# Engineering basics

This pack supplies a starting checklist for a bounded engineering increment. Apply it to the actual project context and record adaptations.

## Requirement quality

Write an observable behavior under specified conditions, with measurable acceptance criteria. Link the need, source, rationale, and verification method. Record unconfirmed limits as assumptions with an owner.

## Evidence quality

Tie results to the tested baseline and environment. Preserve actual output and execution conditions. Distinguish simulation, physical measurement, inspection, and acceptance. A result supports the specific criterion and conditions demonstrated.

## Review quality

Inspect the actual deliverable against its requirements and engineering rules. Record findings with location and reason. Close findings through evidence or an authorized owner disposition. Acceptance applies to a reviewed baseline.

## Reuse quality

Check a lesson's applicability, provenance, assumptions, and limitations before adoption. Keep old evidence against its original baseline; reassess it after relevant changes. Use versioned packs so future sessions can identify the adopted knowledge.

## Origin

These are independently written VeryThinker practices informed by [NASA product realization](https://www.nasa.gov/reference/5-0-product-realization/) and [NASA crosscutting management](https://www.nasa.gov/reference/6-0-crosscutting-technical-management/). They are general engineering guidance, not reproduced process text.
